<div class="content-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="flash-cards">

      <div class="flash-card">
        <h3>How to restore our independence</h3>
        <div class="instruction">First — IGNORE THE SNP IN THE 2024 UK GENERAL ELECTION<br>Instead — repurpose your ballot paper into an independence message</div>
        <p>Voting SNP (or Labour or Tory) will just send more do-nothing representatives from the UK colony of Scotland to Westminster.</p>
        <p>What if instead, all of us who want independence wrote <strong>#endtheunion</strong> across our ballot paper? Spoiled papers are recorded and counted. We could send a direct message from the sovereign people of Scotland.</p>
        <span class="hashtag">#endtheunion</span>
      </div>

      <div class="flash-card">
        <h3>How to restore our independence</h3>
        <div class="instruction">First — STOP THINKING THAT WE HAVE TO ASK<br>Then — stop asking</div>
        <p>Where does it say that we need to ask Westminster's permission?</p>
        <p>Where does it say that we can't simply leave the Union (the UK) anytime we want?</p>
        <p>Where are these rules? You won't find them because they don't exist.</p>
        <span class="hashtag">#endtheunion</span>
      </div>

      <div class="flash-card">
        <h3>How to restore our independence</h3>
        <div class="instruction">First — EDUCATE YOURSELF ON SCOTLAND'S STATUS IN THE UK<br>Then — stop thinking that we have to ask permission</div>
        <p>Scotland and England entered a political union in 1707. The union was forged, and is still governed, by an international treaty, the Treaty of Union.</p>
        <p>There is nothing in the treaty that says either party has to ask to leave the union.</p>
        <span class="hashtag">#endtheunion</span>
      </div>

      <div class="flash-card">
        <h3>How to restore our independence</h3>
        <div class="instruction">First — STOP WISHING FOR ANOTHER INDEPENDENCE REFERENDUM<br>Because we'll never get another one. But mainly because we really, really, don't need one.</div>
        <p>Scotland's people are sovereign. That means that we're in charge — there is no higher authority, and that includes the British parliament.</p>
        <p>So if we're in charge, why would we need to ask anybody?</p>
        <span class="hashtag">#endtheunion</span>
      </div>

      <div class="flash-card">
        <h3>How to restore our independence</h3>
        <div class="instruction">First — ASK WHAT'S BEEN TAKEN FROM SCOTLAND SINCE IT WAS FORCED INTO THE UK IN 1707</div>
        <p>All of Scotland's natural and manufactured resources. All of them.</p>
        <p>The union of Scotland and England was a political and economic union. There's nothing in the treaty that says the British state can pillage and ransack from Scotland anything it damn well wanted. Yet that's exactly what it did. And it's still doing it today.</p>
        <p>Shouldn't we put a stop to that? And then, ask for our money back.</p>
        <span class="hashtag">#endtheunion</span>
      </div>

      <div class="flash-card">
        <h3>How to restore our independence</h3>
        <div class="instruction">First — DON'T BOTHER WITH THE SNP<br>Because the SNP has betrayed you and it has betrayed Scotland.</div>
        <p>In 2015 we elected 56 SNP MPs out of Scotland's 59 MPs.</p>
        <p>But instead of declaring independence, they just got comfortable. Instead of declaring independence, they simpered to the speaker that they were going to be good MPs. They acted their part — representatives of the UK colony of Scotland. They betrayed you.</p>
        <span class="hashtag">#endtheunion</span>
      </div>

      <div class="flash-card">
        <h3>How to restore our independence</h3>
        <div class="instruction">First — IMAGINE ENGLAND WANTED TO LEAVE THE UNION<br>Then — ask who or what would stop it. Scotland?</div>
        <p>Just say, for a moment, that England thought it would be better off outwith the union. It's not such a daft thought. After all, isn't it always saying how much it subsidises Scotland?</p>
        <p>Do you really think that Scottish unionists would have any say whatsoever in stopping England leaving the union?</p>
        <span class="hashtag">#endtheunion</span>
      </div>

    </div>
